From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:12:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] horizon on linux: the draws of a command stream are converted
 and made in C

linux/host/nvnreplay.inc keeps the state a draw reads from the recorded streams and turns each draw into the GPU library's call without Python (the conversion nvn_gpu.py does, ported); the programs, render target images and texture bindings it has not seen are asked of Python once and kept (a texture binding once a frame, so a texture the game wrote since is read again). A draw with storage images, an indirect draw and the other commands Python does itself get the state exported from C. NX2LINUX_NVN_REPLAY=py replays in Python, =check does both and compares every draw.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: NX2Linux S7bis: the replay and conversion of NVN draws in C, off the Python bridge and the GIL
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch swann/jalon-s7bis-xc2)

